# 🌐 Networking Fundamentals

Introduction

Networking is the process of connecting two or more devices so they can communicate and exchange data 
using standard communication protocols over a wired or wireless network.

---

Objectives

The primary objectives of this module are to:

* Understand the fundamentals of computer networking.
* Learn the OSI and TCP/IP networking models.
* Explore commonly used networking protocols and their default port numbers.
* Understand DNS and network communication.
* Configure AWS EC2 Security Groups.
* Practice essential networking commands used in Linux.
* Develop basic network troubleshooting skills.

---

## Why Networking Matters in DevOps

Networking is an essential skill for every DevOps engineer. 
Cloud infrastructure, CI/CD pipelines, containers, virtual machines, APIs, and
microservices all rely on network communication. 
Understanding networking helps in configuring servers, securing cloud environments, diagnosing connectivity problems,
and ensuring reliable application deployment.

---

## Learning Outcomes

After completing this module, you will be able to:

* Explain how data travels across a network.
* Understand the responsibilities of each OSI and TCP/IP layer.
* Identify common networking protocols and their uses.
* Configure AWS Security Groups for secure communication.
* Perform network diagnostics using Linux networking commands.
* Troubleshoot basic networking issues.

